      "defect": "false-claim",
      "evidence": "Step 1.1 justifies the interval partition by saying: \"the powers of $\\varepsilon_D$ are strictly ordered, unbounded above, and their reciprocals are unbounded below.\" But every reciprocal $\\varepsilon_D^{-m}$ is positive because $\\varepsilon_D>1$, so this set is bounded below by $0$. The quoted claim is false as written.",
