    {
      "obligation": "refuter:2:2",
      "id": "thm-negative-pell-period-parity-criterion",
      "location": "[F1]",
      "defect": "citation-inaccurate",
      "evidence": "[F1] attributes to [[thm-square-root-continued-fraction-period-structure]] that \"the state sequence from $\\alpha_1$ onward repeats with least period $\\ell$.\" The cited theorem's Statement says only: \"there is an integer $\\ell\\ge1$ such that $\\sqrt D=[a_0;\\overline{a_1,\\ldots,a_{\\ell-1},2a_0}]$ ... $P_\\ell=a_0,\\ Q_\\ell=1$.\" It does not state leastness. On the current bytes this matters: for $D=2$, the cited statement is satisfied by both $\\ell=1$ and $\\ell=2$, so it does not by itself license the parity-sensitive uses of \"least period\" in steps 2.2 and 3.1.",
      "severity": "fatal",
      "observed_sha256": "04cce439d993f3cc3ea6d68995ac4af802d5ac0d6aa20ec00c5a9e443603a19c"
    },
    {
      "obligation": "refuter:2:3",
      "id": "ex-generalized-pell-bounded-representatives",
      "location": "2.1",
      "defect": "false-claim",
      "evidence": "Step 2.1 claims \"$(8-\\sqrt7)=(8+\\sqrt7)(8+3\\sqrt7)^{-1},\\qquad (13-4\\sqrt7)=(13+4\\sqrt7)(8+3\\sqrt7)^{-1}$\" and concludes that changing the sign of $y$ stays in the same Pell orbit. But $(8+3\\sqrt7)^{-1}=8-3\\sqrt7$, so the products are $(8+\\sqrt7)(8-3\\sqrt7)=43-16\\sqrt7$ and $(13+4\\sqrt7)(8-3\\sqrt7)=20-7\\sqrt7$, not the displayed elements. Thus the asserted orbit identifications are false, and the concluding sentence \"Thus the four representatives are $\\pm(8+\\sqrt7)$ and $\\pm(13+4\\sqrt7)$\" overstates the actual orbit collapse.",
      "severity": "fatal",
      "observed_sha256": "eef4b14ecb49b14d58d45c753e472383c550d926215420d921c35470b87893bf"
    }
